  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal obligations for Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing (NAICS 325412) totaled $106M in FY2027 to date. The market produced 718 awards so far, with an average award size of $147K and obligations down 99.3% year over year. Yearly comparisons show big swings: FY22 obligations were $34.4B, FY23 obligations were $12.8B, FY24 obligations were $10.1B, FY25 obligations were $13.1B, FY26 obligations were $16B, and FY27 obligations were $106M. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer so far, obligating $73.7M, followed by the Department of Justice with $31M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $1M. Vendors with the largest FY2027 to date obligations include MCKESSON CORPORATION at $30.9M, CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC at $15.3M, and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC at $13.4M. The FY2027 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Use these figures to compare contracting activity across prior fiscal years, agencies, and suppliers when deciding whether to pursue opportunities in this NAICS code.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What happened to obligations this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.3% year over year to a total of $106M in FY2027 to date. Award activity produced 718 awards with an average award size of $147K. Prior fiscal years showed much larger totals, for example FY26 obligations were $16B and FY22 obligations were $34.4B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors drive FY2027 to date activity?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer with $73.7M in obligations, followed by the Department of Justice with $31M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $1M. MCKESSON CORPORATION leads vendors with $30.9M, followed by CARDINAL HEALTH 414, LLC with $15.3M and PROGENICS PHARMACEUTICALS INC with $13.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
